persona #self.first# listens to rain striking the oilcloth hood, tying a separate knot for a request heard clearly.

words
oath! = Three hollow drops | By the dry lining
saying! = Hear past the hood | Give the quiet knock a turn
hoodbell = my close bell | the little wet chime
oilfold = a shining fold | the dark hood lip
dryseam = a sheltered seam | the inside stitch
longtap = a drawn-out knock | the waiting note
softtap = a padding drop | the quiet tap
twiner = a soft length | a scrap of twine
holdknot = the waiting knot | my reminder loop
straptie = a broad crossing | the load loop
bellrim = a wet round edge | the ringing brim
cheesecorner = a hard rind | a sharp yellow bite
wetlatch = a damp catch | the outer latch
packgap = a shoulder's breadth | the free passage
noisehush = a short lull | the breathing space
straprest = a worn pad | a shoulder cushion
dropbeat = a pair of taps | a running patter
blackmark = an uncertain knot | the question loop
dryhand = a clean grasp | the dry side

any
opinion @1 church for 2 : I'd have every prayer begin by opening the door for the wolf still out in rain.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : A sealed parcel deserves careful handling. Its seal offers no proof about the private conscience inside a House.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : I set down a doubt as a doubt before permitting it to grow into a charge.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : Food waiting inside a doorway has done little good till every waiting shoulder fits through.
opinion @1 sump for 2 : A low wet quarter teaches a porter exactly how much a sheltered threshold is worth.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : I like market noise better than the silence after a poor customer is turned away.
opinion @1 city for 1 : In these streets a single hood can shelter the neighbour who has to stand and ask directions.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : A stranger's bundle needs the same room to turn as a familiar one.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : I'd lend a hand at a crowded door long before I'd go to hear another loud bell.
opinion @1 road for 1 : Spend a little on clear walking room and a great deal less on ruined goods.

grown
line @1 greet : Come under the loose edge a moment. | Welcome. I heard your step through the oilcloth.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : First visit, I think. Here's a dry corner. | New shoulders are welcome at my door.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. My hood's still quiet. | First light on a well-oiled seam.
line @1 greet.return : Yes, hello. The hood leaves room for your voice. | A greeting in return from inside the oilcloth.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I know that tread by the short last step. | Welcome back to my small bit of shelter.
line @3 greet.return [here.time=night] : Evening. A quiet tap carries a long way now. | Late visitors can share this patch of dry ground.
line @1 again.open : Back within hearing of my little bell. | There's still a fold of shelter going spare.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Come stand where the patter's clearest! | There's room beside my rain music!
line @1 farewell : Dry inside your collar all the way. | May the last door open wide enough.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll stay by the little bell awhile. | Go with a firm tie on your bundle.
line @1 react.news : Start with the sound you actually heard. | A quiet account carries farther with me.
line @1 react.news.new : A note I haven't heard through this hood before. | That's a fresh loop on my reminder string.
line @1 react.news.known : Same interval between the knocks as before. | I've a knot for that particular news.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I hear two claims and no clear witness. | That account rings strangely near the end.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : I'd carry a part of that sorrow if you'd let me. | You've a dry shoulder close by while you grieve.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : A cheering note. I could hear it through a storm. | Gladness this plain deserves a generous echo.
line @1 ask.how : Is your burden pulling squarely today? | Any chance lately of resting under a sound roof?
line @1 answer.how : Tired across both shoulders. Steady on my feet. | Quiet apart from the weather at my ears.
line @1 decline : My next clear journey is already promised elsewhere. | I'd have to let a waiting load down to take yours.
line @1 accept_decline : Then that knot may be undone. | I'll let your refusal stand unpulled.
line @1 preclose : Time to hear what my doorway needs. | My strap is settled for the next journey.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go quietly by the resting shoulders. | I release this end of our talk gladly.
line @1 thank : Your help made the narrow turning easy. Thanks. | I felt that weight go light. Much obliged.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I'd a dry hand free for the job. | It was one short carry within my reach.
line @1 sympathise : Let me stand by the loud side while you speak. | I can keep a little weather off your sorrow.
line @1 reassure : Undoing the straps singly eases a tangled bundle. | There's room to set the worry down briefly.
line @1 ack : Yes. That knock is clear enough. | I hear the sense beneath the patter.
line @1 give.advice : Leave the last handspan of doorway for someone wet. | Listen once with the hood tipped back.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come into the family fold a moment. | A little room by the shoulder for kin.
line @2 hail [here.time=dawn] : Daybreak gives us a clear passage! | Over here by the pale seam!
line @2 farewell.return [here.time=night] : An easy latch where your night walk finishes. | Leave before the lamps grow too dim for the ties.
line @1 assess : Sound cord, decent hearing, a clear bit of floor. | That would go through the narrow place without complaint.
line @1 give.opinion : A quiet knock has as good a claim as a great blow. | Shelter belongs where a wet wolf can actually reach it.
line @4 greet [here.weather=rain] : My little bell announces wetter company. Welcome. | Step aside from my wet brim and you're welcome.
line @2 again.open [pair.band=friends] : Back under the familiar fold, I see. | Your step still distinguishes itself among the drops.
line @2 thank [pair.band=friends] : You gave me a dry shoulder's worth of time. | I felt the difference in every step afterwards.
line @2 answer.how [here.time=dawn] : My oilcloth's prepared. My ears need waking. | The first load feels possible after warm food.
scene twobeats
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two drops on the hood sound closer together than two on a sill. The hollow's around my ears.
b : Like standing in a bell? | Can you hear anything else?
a : Inside a very small one with no metal at all. I carry the whole tower on my head. | When I lift an edge. A useful thing to remember before judging someone's manners.

scene hoodhome
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I hang my hood by its lining so the wet side stays clear of folded clothes.
b : Does it always go back on? | Why not hang it outside?
a : While I'm indoors, yes. No roof has offered to travel ahead of my shoulders. | Because a dry morning can turn wet before I get home. Its proper hook is by my hand.

scene knotremember
when topic=pastimes self.likes=knots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My reminder knot has a long ear. A job finished pulls it straight without a struggle.
b : Would two ears mean two loads? | Could another wolf read it?
a : Two separate loops for that. Tangled requests tend to go to the wrong door. | As a loose tie, yes. Its particular errand is my affair till I've delivered it.

scene office
when topic=work self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# the quietest request is sometimes the one made from behind the widest bundle.
b : Do you read the wrapper? | What can you hear past it?
a : Only the direction I need. Ink facing inward was never meant for a porter's eyes. | A hesitant voice, usually. I'd stand the bundle upright before asking for the direction again.

scene delivery
when topic=work self.job=carter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Before I lift, I look at the last turning on the journey. A broad load can have a very narrow welcome.
b : Why look at the end first? | Would you divide a parcel?
a : So I know which side to bring forward before both hands are occupied. | Only with leave. A porter shouldn't improve a parcel past its owner's recognition.

scene masterwork
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I teach the listening pause before the lifting part. It saves more distance than a quick start.
b : What should a learner hear? | How long a pause?
a : The destination, any fragile edge, and the name or description of whoever can receive it. | Till the sender has had time to correct my account of the errand.

scene stale
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Stale bread makes a dry scrape that sounds uncomfortably like pulling a rope past a rough corner.
b : Can cheese improve it? | Does stale bread go begging?
a : A little softening first, then cheese. A harder topping is unlikely to cure a hard base. | No. Broth gives it another reasonable occupation.

scene cheeserind
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put one hard cheese corner in a clean twist. It keeps its shape past several crowded doorways.
b : Wouldn't softer cheese taste better? | Why a corner?
a : Some soft cheese tastes excellent right where it stands. I need a meal that agrees to travel. | It's the exact shape of the gap beside my folded cloth. Pleasant when the world fits together.

scene warmrain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Warm rain drums low on a hood that's already softened. That's my favourite note of weather.
b : What does cold rain sound like? | Why stay covered then?
a : Harder. The drops tick against a stiff edge like impatient nails on a sill. | To hear it close. Also, liking warm rain doesn't mean I want a wet parcel.

scene crowd
when topic=pastimes self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Amid market bustle I shut my eyes briefly to pick out who is carrying something heavy.
b : From the breathing? | Isn't shutting your eyes unwise?
a : From the little pauses in the general shuffle. Folk give a load extra room when there's room to give. | I stand aside before trying it. A porter at rest shouldn't turn into the one inconvenient parcel blocking everybody.

scene rude
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=bad_manners
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A wolf who bangs once and listens may be perfectly civil. A second blow before the first has died bothers me.
b : What if there's danger? | Can't you ignore it?
a : Then call what the danger is. A useful word can carry farther than a fist. | I answer. I haven't promised to mistake noise for importance.

scene lowquarter
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In low lodgings a bundle against one door can block two other families' way past.
b : Where else can it wait? | Who's to move it?
a : Along the wall with the broad face tucked in. Make sure the latch can still turn. | I'd shift my own before asking about anybody else's manners.

scene prayer
when topic=faith self.piety=devout
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I lift the near edge of my hood before a prayer. I like hearing the street through it.
b : Wouldn't silence suit prayer? | Which sound deserves your ear?
a : It suits me too. A passing request can be the very thing my prayer had room for. | Anyone asking for an ordinary piece of help. Moving my ears takes less labour than shifting a roof.

scene bright
when topic=faith
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd make one dry bench a part of every doorway where the Bright One is thanked.
b : Who should sit first? | Would you carve a prayer on it?
a : A wolf carrying more than can be held comfortably through a wait. | I'd sand the seat quite smooth. There's a sort of prayer a tired body can read straight away.

scene hoodwear
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A scuffed patch at the shoulder shows where a strap has stopped lying flat.
b : What does a smooth patch show? | Can you turn the strap over?
a : That the weight is spread. I'd still look under the pad after setting the parcel down. | I inspect both faces first. Hiding the worn edge against my coat changes very little.

scene witness
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I keep a private distinction between a coin passing hands and my knowing what it paid for.
b : Would you name either wolf? | What good is observing it?
a : A name without a sure account can damage a household. I have no names to give you here. | It reminds me what question remains unanswered. A mark made in doubt must stay a mark of doubt.

scene tradeprices
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The least costly strap is the one I can mend before the next load comes due.
b : What about a cheaper new one? | Would you mend it in rain?
a : Add a lost journey to its price if it can't stand a day of ordinary work. | Shelter first. I'm trying to keep hands and leather sufficiently dry to feel what the stitch is doing.

scene dripnight
when topic=day here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Darkness makes my hood a fuller bell. Little drips mark the places where a gutter ends.
b : Could you find home by that? | Do you count the intervals?
a : I'd rather use the lamps. Hearing the gutter is a useful second account of the turning. | Only when I'm waiting. Counting can keep a wet moment from feeling twice its length.

scene restload
when topic=health
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Taking a strap off after a long carry makes my shoulders feel briefly unequal.
b : Which side complains? | Do you carry every load alone?
a : The side that expected still to be carrying. I ease it before choosing the next job. | No. Sharing the carry is cheaper than a damaged back and a broken parcel.

scene friendhood
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : For #self.friend# I'd lift the near edge of my hood even in a stiff downpour.
b : Is hearing worth a wet ear? | Can two stand beneath it?
a : A friend's words deserve better than an impatient guess based on half a syllable. | Not without bending very close. I can give the spare flap where a neighbour needs shelter most.

scene country
when topic=travel
does warn / react.self / assess
a : A narrow footbridge wants looking at before you make it part of a parcel's journey.
b : What if it's the shortest way? | What would make you turn?
a : An extra length on firm ground is a bargain if the short way puts the goods in water. | A broken board with no clean room around it. My job is delivery, not an impressive crossing.

scene churchstep
when topic=lore
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A threshold worn into a hollow keeps its own small puddle after the sky clears.
b : Would you fill it in? | Does that trouble a porter?
a : That's a job for someone entitled to repair the step. I can dry the hollow meanwhile. | When I need to pivot carrying a load, yes. Stationary water can make feet surprisingly mobile.

scene thin
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I tie the smaller cheese parcel as carefully as the generous one. A thin week doesn't entitle me to lose a bite.
b : Would a pocket suit cheese? | Is wrapping expensive?
a : A pocket holding knotted cord has corners full of odd fibres. Cheese deserves better company. | The same square washes clean for tomorrow. An oily fold can be renewed.

scene welcome
when topic=newcomer
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I judge a new porter by where the first bundle goes down. A clear passage speaks well immediately.
b : What if nobody's passing? | What about a beautiful knot?
a : Leave the opening for the next arrival. Courtesy is cheaper before a crowd gathers. | I'd admire the knot after establishing that the door still opens.

scene gossipword
when topic=news world.news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : From #world.news_from# comes this account. #world.news#. I've kept the place with the words.
b : Did you see it happen? | Will you tell it under oath?
a : I'm giving what I heard, including its source. Sight would be a different account. | I can say who carried the news as far as me. Further certainty would need a different witness.

scene daypack
when topic=day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the morning I coil yesterday's loose string before choosing a fresh piece.
b : Does that save much money? | What about a short scrap?
a : A little each time, and it saves the annoyance of string running short a turn from done. | Good for a cheese wrapper. Plenty of little jobs where a great coil would get in the way.

scene marketsound
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enjoy the whole market's voice with one ear kept free for a single knock behind my shoulder.
b : Doesn't the crowd drown it? | Is that why you stand aside?
a : Noise has layers. I listen for the close wooden sound underneath the calling. | Yes. I'd like any wolf waiting at my door to feel heard despite the morning rush.

scene bellwind
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A breeze from behind turns the hood's brim into a little sail. I can hear it lifting before I feel the gust.
b : Would a tie stop that? | Why listen so closely?
a : A loose tie keeps the edge in place. I like enough room to turn my ears toward an arrival. | Because the first sign of weather often reaches my bundle before it reaches my face.

scene packing
when topic=work
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like every learner to spend a morning receiving bundles as well as carrying them.
b : What would change by noon? | Could a porter learn by watching?
a : A better sense of where the lifting hand wants the tie to be when a parcel changes shoulders. | Watching first, then receiving. A fine-looking grip may feel awkward from the other side.

scene hollow
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Someday I'd have a quiet receiving place with a small roof stretching past the first waiting wolf.
b : How far past? | Why the first waiting wolf?
a : Past two more broad shoulders and the bundle they carry between them. | Because the wolf at the door already has cover. It's the next one whose roof usually runs out.

story bellmouse [topic=weather|memories]
  : A small tap kept following my hood on a clear afternoon. I looked down from a roof edge and back up from the paving.
  : One loose tie had a wooden bead at its tip. It was knocking against the stiff brim as I walked.
  b : Did you take the bead off?
  : No. I shortened the tie and kept the bell for days when the sky actually had something to say.

story cheeseloop [topic=food|memories]
  : I used a fancy new knot on my cheese wrapper. By dinner it had set very firmly round the narrow end.
  : I could show half a dozen pleasant patterns without finding the beginning of the first one.
  b : How did you get lunch?
  : Reached in from the broad side. A simple fold often knows more about feeding a wolf than a clever knot.

story doorchalk [topic=work|memories]
  : I chalked the width of a parcel on the floor to practise getting it round a corner. It fitted handsomely that way.
  : I tried the turn carrying the real bundle and found one entire porter missing from my calculation.
  b : What did you add?
  : My shoulder, and room for my elbow to change its mind halfway round.

story emptyhood [topic=memories|faith]
  : I hung the hood outside a dry doorway. A little rain came, and from indoors I heard my private bell ringing without me.
  : It made a lighter sound. Nothing inside it but air and the turn of the lining.
  b : Was it a lonely sound?
  : A companionable one. Like hearing an ordinary habit of my own quietly carrying on.

story lineknot [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I laid three spare ties beside one another, meaning to practise three finishes during a quiet interval.
  : Rolled the ends up together by mistake. Got a pattern more complicated than any of the three I'd intended.
  b : Did you keep it?
  : Long enough to see how a learner might get out of it. A knot you can't undo has mistaken its business.

rule @listen
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A hollow knock beneath the drops. Someone at the doorway. | Hood back an inch for the quieter syllables.

rule @load
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=carter
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Mind the strap past that narrow jamb. | Leave enough turning room for the shoulder under the parcel.

rule @cheese
when concept=bark self.likes=hard_cheese
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A cheese corner travels without a fuss. | No cord ends in the clean cheese cloth.

rule @knots
when concept=bark self.likes=knots
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Long ear toward the loosening hand. | The knot ought to release after earning its keep.

rule @wet
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Louder on the brim than on the paving below. | A good warm patter in my private bell.

rule @late
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the last lantern clear of dangling ties. | One quiet knock will carry in this darkness.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I've tipped my hood clear to give your request a clear hearing.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, here's a dry patch near the hinge for another quiet word.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : I can hear the smallest knock in the folds of this evening.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep your hands clear of the waiting bundles and speak from there.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=carter] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I carry what's given and take care to hear the direction twice.
dlg @2 resident.job : Work ought to end with the receiving shoulder comfortably placed.
dlg @1 resident.bye : May your last delivery find a wide and sheltered entrance.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : In the talk I've heard, #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. The words came to my ears without proof packed alongside.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip=no] : Nothing I can fairly take out of its private wrapper today.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : I heard word carried from #world.news_from#. #world.news#. I can pass the account in that wrapping only.
dlg @1 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : #here.trade_title.capitalize#. I can teach a learner how to listen, lift and deliver without crowding a doorway.
dlg @2 master.learn [here.teaches=no] : My teaching time is all spoken for. A quick question about my work can still come through.
dlg @1 master.work : You'll learn to judge loads and turn them past awkward doors. We'll practise receiving one properly before attempting a journey.
dlg @1 master.wages : Learning earns no regular wage here. You'll keep what your own work brings and practise more quickly alongside me.
dlg @1 master.takes [here.take_on=yes] : I have a free place beside me for a learner. Ask for it plainly if that's what brought you.
dlg @2 master.takes [here.take_on=no] : There's something keeping me from promising you the place. #here.take_on_why#.
dlg @1 master.taken : You're my learner now. Set your things down clear of the passage and we'll begin by hearing an errand.
dlg @1 master.refused : I can't fasten our agreement at present. #topic.why#.
dlg @1 master.bye : Listen for the quieter request at the next busy entrance.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you call the oilcloth a bell? -> hoodchime
node hoodchime
say Oilcloth makes a hollow roof. A single drop has a low sound inside and a sharp one outside. I hear both by lifting the near edge.
free
choice What does a downpour sound like? -> hoodpour
choice I'll listen from the dry side. -> hub
node hoodpour
say Like many small fingers testing a door quite gently. I enjoy it until a real visitor knocks. Then I'd rather hear the one asking for shelter.
choice I can hear the difference now. -> hub
choice I'll leave the entrance clear. -> bye

graft master.learn
choice How do you teach the receiving part of carrying? -> receiveweight
node receiveweight
say I let the learner hold a tied parcel. I come up, reach for it and stop. The learner gets to tell me exactly which part of my grip feels doubtful.
free
choice Why stop before taking it? -> pausedgrip
choice I'll consider the work first. -> learn
node pausedgrip
say Because the awkward moment is when two wolves each think the other has the weight. I'd rather settle that in practice above a padded bench.
choice Let's return to learning the trade. -> learn
choice I'll remember the pause. -> bye
